@model string?
@* A read that failed, said out loud.

   Every surface already degrades one source at a time and renders what it could read, which is
   the right behaviour — but a panel that is empty because Azure was unreachable looks exactly
   like a panel that is empty because there is nothing to report, and on a console someone makes
   decisions from those two must not look alike. "No denials" and "we could not ask" are opposite
   findings.

   Deliberately not an alert, and deliberately not a retry: the clients give up in seconds
   (ClientRegistration.Budget) precisely so the operator gets an answer and can decide whether to
   refresh, rather than watching a page hang while a library works through its backoff. *@
@if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Model))
{
    <partial name="_Banner" model="@(new BannerModel("⚠️", Model + " — refresh to try again."))" />
}
